Subject: [PATCH] binder: enable cached-app freezer ioctl support

The LineageOS 23.2 sm8350 binder driver contains the Binder process-freezer
implementation, but compiles out both the implementation helpers and ioctl
handlers with #if 0. Android 16's framework probes BINDER_GET_FROZEN_INFO
when checking freezer support and uses BINDER_FREEZE to coordinate pending
Binder transactions before a process is frozen.

Enable the existing implementation rather than duplicating or replacing it.

--- a/drivers/android/binder.c
+++ b/drivers/android/binder.c
@@ -5540,1 +5540,0 @@
-#if 0
@@ -5688,1 +5687,0 @@
-#endif
@@ -5808,1 +5806,0 @@
-#if 0
@@ -5887,1 +5884,0 @@
-#endif
